// expect-error: aborting due to 4 previous errors
//
// A syntax error `fatal` gives up on drops the statement it is in, not the function around it. One
// function with four broken statements reports each once: parsing resumed at the next line of the same
// block, so none is a cascade of the one before. Before, the first broken statement dropped the whole
// function and the other three were never read.
//
// The `if` drops its body with it (the braces it opened are counted, and its `}` is not mistaken for the
// block's own); the last is the half-typed line at the end of a block, where the closing brace is the
// block's own and the function after it still parses.

